@page "/privacy"
<PageTitle>Privacy — Interlock Expeditions</PageTitle>
<article class="prose"><h1>Privacy</h1><h2>Room access</h2><p>Your host account manages its rooms. Joined players see their own crew's clues, the shared controls, nicknames and room activity. Anyone with an invitation can join while space remains.</p><p>Keep your account recovery key private. Sharing an invitation does not share your account or existing player access. Nicknames are not verified identities.</p><h2>What is saved</h2><p>We store account nicknames, room settings and progress, player nicknames, actions and reports. The site operator can access stored room data. We do not request a camera, microphone, location or contacts.</p><p>Sign-in and player access are saved on your device. Clearing site data can lose player access; a host can sign in again with the recovery key. Progress stays with the room.</p><h2>Delete your data</h2><p>A host can end and delete a room, including its players, progress, reports and activity. Deleting the host account deletes its rooms and sessions. An open checkout or active paid period must end first.</p><p>Up to fifty rooms can be kept per host. Deletion removes the active records; hosting providers may retain operational backups.</p><h2>Reports and payment</h2><p>A report stores the reason and note you submit. Do not include recovery keys or unrelated personal details. Sending a report does not automatically remove another player.</p><p>Network-derived identifiers help limit abuse. Diagnostics record action status and timing without raw credentials or submitted machine settings. Card details are handled by the payment provider when checkout is available. This release loads no advertising scripts.</p><details><summary>Public source and story answers</summary><p>The source includes the fictional stories and puzzle solutions. It does not include real room records or private account keys.</p></details></article>
